1
-- 1. :silent! does not abort the loop
still here n=1
still here n=2
still here n=3
n=3 errmsg=E730: Using a List as a String
-- 2. a caught error does not abort the loop
caught Vim(echo):E730: Using a List as a String
caught Vim(echo):E730: Using a List as a String
caught Vim(echo):E730: Using a List as a String
n=3
-- 3. an UNCAUGHT error inside a :try around the loop still stops the loop
caught Vim(echo):E730: Using a List as a String
n=1
-- 4. an error inside a plain function does not abort the caller
E730: Using a List as a String
the plain body carries on
E730: Using a List as a String
the plain body carries on
E730: Using a List as a String
the plain body carries on
n=3
-- 5. ... but an `abort` function stops its own body AND the caller
E730: Using a List as a String
n=1
-- 6. a lambda is not a do_cmdline: its error DOES stop the caller
E730: Using a List as a String
n=1